        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-08T16:42:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could definitely use a second interface to deliver ISH-\u003eAP message (e.g. EC_MKBP_EVENT_SENSOR_FIFO)\n\nThe other option is to register another client for the ISH-\u003eAP message and remove this header completely.\n\nHowever, there is a precedent for a protocol specific header, see i2c implementation for cros_ec command interface.\n\nI lean to keeping the ishtp message header (it also makes it more consistent with other ishtp clients in the wild - which seems somewhat helpful)",
      "parentUuid": "32b972da_4e38168c",
      "revId": "690e4afe1ee596169a284c02a3d2263771e19786",
